 "text": "-->\nREGISTER OF DEEDS | perkinscounty\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nHOME\nDEPARTMENTS\nDRIVER LICENSES\nCLERK OF COURTS\nDIRECTOR OF EQUALIZATION\nFINANCE OFFICE (Auditor/Treasurer)\nTAX DEEDS\nHIGHWAY\nREGISTER OF DEEDS\nSHERIFF/EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT\nSTATES ATTORNEY\nVETERANS OFFICE\nWEED AND PEST\nPREDATOR CONTROL\n4-H\nCOMMISSIONERS\n2026 Meeting Minutes\nLEGAL NOTICES\nGIS & PLAT MAP\nORGANIZED TOWNSHIP PORTAL\nELECTIONS\nPROPERTY TAX RELIEF PROGRAMS\nARCHIVE LEGAL NOTICES\nABOUT US\nJOB OPPORTUNITIES\nMORE PORTALS\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nRegister of Deeds\nPO Box 127\nBison, SD 57620\n605-244-5620 (phone)\n605-231-5560 (fax)\nHeidi Stevens - Register of Deeds\nAmanda Larson - Deputy Register of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds is the elected official county record keeper. The Register of Deeds issues and files marriage licenses, birth and death certificates, burial permits, real estate transactions (including deeds, mortgages and mortgage transfers), federal and state tax liens, state unemployment tax, military discharge records, businesses and new business. The Register of Deeds is also responsible for survey plat certificates and county welfare liens.\nChecklist for recording instruments\nList of Exemptions from Real Estate Transfer Fees\nList of Fees\nCertificate of Real Estate Value\nRecording Standards\nbottom of page",
